#: libs/word-tiles-client-ts/src/word-tiles-game-client.tsx
msgid "Take turns placing tiles from your seven-tile rack in one row or column to form words, joined to the tiles already on the 15 × 15 board; the first word covers the centre star. Every word you form or extend must be in the word list, and each is scored: letter squares multiply the new tile under them, word squares the whole word, and using all seven tiles earns 50 more. A blank plays any letter for no points. Instead of placing you may pass, or exchange tiles while the bag holds at least seven. The game ends when someone uses their last tile with the bag empty — the others' remaining tiles count against them and go to that player — or after six scoreless turns in a row, when everyone's remaining tiles count against them. The highest score wins; tied leaders share the win. Resigning or running out of time follows the table's rules: with two players the other wins, with more the game is drawn. Word list: {lexicon} (ENABLE, public domain, words of 2 to 15 letters). Rules: {ruleset}."
msgstr "Take turns placing tiles from your seven-tile rack in one row or column to form words, joined to the tiles already on the 15 × 15 board; the first word covers the centre star. Every word you form or extend must be in the word list, and each is scored: letter squares multiply the new tile under them, word squares the whole word, and using all seven tiles earns 50 more. A blank plays any letter for no points. Instead of placing you may pass, or exchange tiles while the bag holds at least seven. The game ends when someone uses their last tile with the bag empty — the others' remaining tiles count against them and go to that player — or after six scoreless turns in a row, when everyone's remaining tiles count against them. The highest score wins; tied leaders share the win. Resigning or running out of time follows the table's rules: with two players the other wins, with more the game is drawn. Word list: {lexicon} (ENABLE, public domain, words of 2 to 15 letters). Rules: {ruleset}."

