msgid "This hill variant uses a nine-by-nine board and five walls per player. South starts at e1, West at a5, North at e9 and East at i5. Turns run in that clockwise order. Move or place a wall; jump one pawn, never a chain. A blocked landing allows a side-step. Walls must keep everyone's path to e5 open. Reaching e5 wins immediately; no holding period. A withdrawal or expired clock ends the round as a draw. If no pawn move or wall is legal, pass when offered; you cannot pass otherwise."
msgstr "This hill variant uses a nine-by-nine board and five walls per player. South starts at e1, West at a5, North at e9 and East at i5. Turns run in that clockwise order. Move or place a wall; jump one pawn, never a chain. A blocked landing allows a side-step. Walls must keep everyone's path to e5 open. Reaching e5 wins immediately; no holding period. A withdrawal or expired clock ends the round as a draw. If no pawn move or wall is legal, pass when offered; you cannot pass otherwise."

